From d2952267d55d2eb718df8108164d830f4b1ca03a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco <mpalinar@nmblr.ai>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 06:37:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] Add explicit Metal device selection for multi-GPU Intel
 Macs

Upstream calls MTLCreateSystemDefaultDevice(), which is correct on Apple
Silicon where exactly one Metal GPU exists. On an Intel Mac with an eGPU
there are two or more, and which one is the system default depends on
macOS GPU selection policy and which display is attached.

This adds a shared selector honouring H3_METAL_DEVICE_NAME,
H3_METAL_DEVICE_INDEX and H3_METAL_REGISTRY_ID, and routes BOTH
independent device-creation paths (the --info probe in h3_metal.m and the
inference context in h3_gpu.m) through it, so they can never disagree.

With no environment variable set the behaviour is identical to upstream.
When an explicit request cannot be satisfied the selector returns nil and
lists the available devices, rather than silently running a 33B video
model on an Intel UHD 630.
---
 Makefile           |   2 +-
 h3_device_select.h |  35 +++++++++++++
 h3_device_select.m | 120 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 h3_gpu.m           |   3 +-
 h3_metal.m         |   5 +-
 5 files changed, 162 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 h3_device_select.h
 create mode 100644 h3_device_select.m

